#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# continued_fraction_k

#% text
# `continued_fraction_k(f, g, [i, imin, imax])` gives the finite continued fraction `f(imin)/(g(imin) + f(imin + 1)/(g(imin + 1) + ...))` ending at `imax`; `continued_fraction_k(g, [i, imin, imax])` takes every numerator 1; `[i, imax]` means `[i, 1, imax]`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
continued_fraction_k(n^2, [n, 1, 10])
#% output
#= 13690825314204/17021645372933

#% cell
continued_fraction_k(a(n), b(n), [n, 3])
#% output
#= a(1)/(b(1) + a(2)/(b(2) + a(3)/b(3)))

#% cell
continued_fraction_k(1, [k, 8])
#% output
#= 21/34

#% text
# An infinite fraction with constant terms converges to the root of `K^2 + g K - f = 0` of smaller modulus (here `f = 1`, `g = 1`: the golden ratio minus 1):

#% cell
continued_fraction_k(1, [n, 1, inf])
#% output
#= (1/2)*(-1 + 5^(1/2))

